# Opm CLI Reference

File: opm/docs/cli.oot

opm is the openOODA package manager. Entry is `opm <subcommand>`.
`ooda` may wrap this; that wrap lives in the ooda repo.

## 1. Top-Level Command

The dispatcher is `cli/main.oo`. It parses `argv[0]` as the subcommand
and routes rest plus `&FsReadCap`, `&FsWriteCap`, `&ProcessCap`,
`&EnvCap` to the handler. Unknown subcommand prints help and exits 2.

Every subcommand is fail-closed.

## 2. Subcommand Index

Live commands (help lists only these):

| Subcommand | Purpose | Handler |
|---|---|---|
| `add` | Resolve and install packages | `cli/cmd_add.oo` |
| `audit` | Walk the lock against yank, advisory, and pins | `cli/cmd_audit.oo` |
| `sbom` | CycloneDX-lite from the lock | `cli/cmd_audit.oo` |
| `bot` | Verify a registry folder and write catalog | `cli/cmd_bot.oo` |
| `ingest` | Lock a file-backed recipe | `cli/cmd_ingest.oo` |
| `init` | Write a starter `ooda.pkg` | `cli/cmd_init.oo` |
| `launch` | Re-verify and optionally run a pinned payload | `cli/cmd_launch.oo` |
| `remove` | Drop a package from the lock | `cli/cmd_ops.oo` |
| `update` | Re-resolve and refresh the lock | `cli/cmd_ops.oo` |
| `outdated` | List newer compatible versions | `cli/cmd_ops.oo` |
| `why` | Print why a package is in the lock | `cli/cmd_ops.oo` |
| `pack` | Build an offline pack from the lock | `cli/cmd_pack.oo` |
| `pkg` | Print the current lock | `cli/cmd_pkg.oo` |
| `publish` | Write manifest + payload to a local registry tree | `cli/cmd_publish.oo` |
| `reg`, `registry`, `regs` | List or edit HTTPS stores | `cli/cmd_regs.oo` |
| `search` | Search added stores by substring | `cli/cmd_search.oo` |
| `tree` | Print a dep tree | `cli/cmd_tree.oo` |
| `vendor` | List the file vendor | `cli/cmd_tree.oo` |
| `clean` | Drop CAS dirs not in the lock | `cli/cmd_tree.oo` |

Helpers (not commands): `catalog.oo`, `argv.oo`, `slurp.oo`,
`vendor_pick.oo`, `git_clone.oo`, `reg_fetch.oo`.

## 3. Aliases

- `reg`, `registry` → `regs`
- `vendor`, `clean` are their own names, not tree flags

`sbom` is not an alias of `audit`.

## 4. Common Flags

- `--json` — machine object instead of text
- `--vendor <path>` — file vendor directory
- `--from <dir>` — local directory recipe

HTTPS fetch needs `OODA_CURL`. Git clone needs `OODA_GIT`.
Minisign needs `OODA_MINISIGN`. Compiler spawn needs `OODA_COMPILER`.
Writes need `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`. Missing token is Err.

## 5. Notes

`init [name]` reads the name from rest[0]. Default name is `pkg`.

`launch <name> [--exec]` re-hashes CAS. `--exec` runs `oodac run`
on the pinned `.oo`. `OODA_UNTRUSTED` refuses exec.

`add` refuses extra caps. That is the unique move. Do not add
helper names as user commands.

## 6. Exit Codes

- `0` — success
- `1` — manifest or payload missing
- `2` — bad name, yank, license, cap, sha, sig, or pin miss

Scripts treat any non-zero as a hard fail.
